# The recorded checks compare bytes, and the expected render is read from the working tree. If a
# developer's core.autocrlf handed them a CRLF copy, `--golden check` would fail for a reason that
# has nothing to do with the change under review. Pinning the whole package to LF removes that.
#
# The fixture journal is line-ending independent when parsed (the reader splits on /\r?\n/), but it
# is pinned too so a fresh clone on any platform gets byte-identical input.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated, and large: keep them out of diffs and out of language statistics.
test/fixtures/golden/golden-session.expected.md linguist-generated=true -diff
test/fixtures/golden/golden-session.digest.json linguist-generated=true -diff
